from pathlib import Path
import json,html
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
states=json.loads((p/'states.json').read_text())['states']; sections=[]
def math(tex,display=True):
 return '<div class="equation" data-tex="'+html.escape(tex,quote=True)+'"></div>' if display else '<span data-tex="'+html.escape(tex,quote=True)+'"></span>'
for n in sorted({s['n'] for s in states}):
 rows=[s for s in states if s['n']==n]
 out=f'<details><summary>{n} qubits · exact orders '+', '.join(str(s['achievedOrder']) for s in rows)+'</summary>'
 for s in rows:
  w=s['verification']['nextOrderWitness'];q=w['order']
  eq=r'\left(\rho_{%d}-\frac{I_{%d}}{%d}\right)_{%d,%d}=%s\ne0'%(q,q+1,q+1,w['row'],w['column'],w['differenceLatex'])
  out+=f'<h3 id="n{n}-t{s["achievedOrder"]}">Exactly {s["achievedOrder"]}-AC</h3>'+math(s['stateLatex'])+math(eq)
 sections.append(out+'</details>')
(p/'index.html').write_text(r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>States with exactly the requested AC order</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><script src="page.js" defer></script><style>main{max-width:1000px;padding-block:38px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin:32px 0 16px}.equation{overflow-x:auto;padding:15px 0}details{padding:18px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}h3{margin-top:25px}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;margin-block:25px}</style></head><body><main><a href="../../index.html">← Anticoherent-state catalogue</a><p class="eyebrow">Exact constructions</p><h1>Exactly t-anticoherent states</h1><p>The existence table asks whether a state is at least <span data-tex="t"></span>-AC. Lower-order cells now default to a representative with exactly the requested order. Each new state below satisfies <span data-tex="\rho_t=I_{t+1}/(t+1)"></span>, while an explicitly nonzero entry proves <span data-tex="\rho_{t+1}\ne I_{t+2}/(t+2)"></span>. By nesting, that representative cannot have any higher AC order. This does not bound the order of other states at the same qubit number.</p><p><a href="general/index.html">General analytical construction for every sufficiently large N, with an explicit bound and proof ↗</a></p><h2>Construction and proof</h2><p>Choose excitation indices separated by more than <span data-tex="t"></span>, and positive rational weights matching the first <span data-tex="t"></span> moments of the uniform distribution on <span data-tex="0,\ldots,n"></span>:</p><div class="equation" data-tex="|\psi\rangle=\sum_i\sqrt{w_i}|D_n^{(r_i)}\rangle,\qquad\sum_iw_i r_i^q=\frac1{n+1}\sum_{r=0}^n r^q\quad(0\le q\le t)."></div><p>The support gaps eliminate the off-diagonal entries of every reduction through order <span data-tex="t"></span>. Each diagonal entry is an expectation of a polynomial of degree at most <span data-tex="t"></span> in the excitation index. Matching the uniform moments makes it equal to the reduction of the symmetric identity, namely <span data-tex="1/(t+1)"></span>.</p><p>First-order cells use GHZ states. Two fourth-order cases use phase freedom: the eighteen-qubit state removes the phases of the existing fifth-order witness; the sixteen-qubit state uses a minus sign on its excitation-12 component to cancel fourth-order coherences. Their full reduced matrices are verified directly, without the support-gap argument.</p><h2>Independent exact verification</h2><p>A separate verifier constructs the Schmidt matrix</p><div class="equation" data-tex="M^{(q)}_{ab}=c_{a+b}\sqrt{\frac{\binom qa\binom{n-q}b}{\binom n{a+b}}},\qquad\rho_q=M^{(q)}M^{(q)\dagger}."></div><p>It checks normalization, all reductions through the claimed order, the next-order nonzero entry and the saved squared Frobenius distance. All calculations use exact symbolic arithmetic. Matrix indices below start at zero. There are 49 new witnesses; pre-existing exact-order examples remain in the catalogue.</p><div class="downloads"><a href="states.json">Exact states ↓</a><a href="verification.json">Verification report ↓</a><a href="verify.py">Independent verifier ↓</a><a href="build.py">Construction script ↓</a></div><h2>Analytical examples</h2>'''+''.join(sections)+'''</main></body></html>''')
(p/'page.js').write_text("document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]').forEach(el=>katex.render(el.dataset.tex,el,{displayMode:el.classList.contains('equation'),throwOnError:false}));});\n")
